each foot has 250,000 sweat glands and  can produce two cups of sweat per day  sweat itself is odorless but poorly  ventilated shoes is a perfect place for  bacteria to grow and bacteria is where  the smell comes from when sleeping many  of our bodily functions stop or slow  down including saliva production it is  estimated that the average human  produces 6 cups of saliva daily however  during sleep saliva production drops to  nearly zero halting your mouths natural  process of removing food particles  [Music]  armpits contain up to 1 million bacteria  per square centimetre the smell comes  from bacteria eating skin cells and  metabolizing sweat the same sweat glands  in your armpits are also in your ear  canal people who have wet earwax are  more prone to smelly armpit  [Music]  farting is the body's way of releasing  excess gas that builds up in the  intestines throughout the day if the gas  stays in the intestines for an extended  period of time  bacteria can add sulfates which can  contribute to the smell eating foods  high in sulfur such as cheese broccoli  garlic and beans can cause the farts to  become smelly the average person  releases gas 15 times a day that  averages to one part every hour and a  half but it's okay we're all human  [Music]
 

